  "title": "The Kiosk Ate My Points. I Built A Folder.",
  "script": "Our neighborhood pizza chain made us redeem rewards only through a kiosk that glitched constantly, then support blamed user error whenever it ate points. Mine vanished the week I hit a free pizza. So I started screenshotting every glitch\u2014mine and four strangers'\u2014that same week. I built a shared folder, found the chain's consumer complaints email in its privacy policy, and sent corporate a timeline with timestamps. Three weeks later, the chain announced a loyalty audit. It restored six months of missing points to every account with a ticket and fired the vendor running the kiosks. I got my free pizza, slightly cold, which felt appropriate. Forty-two strangers got theirs too. None knew who started the folder. The kiosk's final reward was paperwork.",
